WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:53.680
<b>Showdown at Alubarna</b>

3
00:01:57.800 --> 00:01:58.770
And that's when it happened!

4
00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:01.140
I looked him straight in the eye and yelled,

5
00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:04.040
"You bowlegged bastard!"

6
00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:05.510
And ever since that day,

7
00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:07.010
crabs throughout
the world have been

8
00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:08.950
self-conscious about
being bowlegged.

9
00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:10.080
Oh!

10
00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:12.370
That's the reason they walk sideways?

11
00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:14.100
Yep.
And at that pivotal moment,

12
00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:15.870
a lobster happened
to be within earshot

13
00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:17.600
and heard the whole thing!

14
00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:19.400
Oh.

15
00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:21.000
So lobsters are crabs too?

16
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.440
Better believe it!

17
00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:23.740
Oh!

18
00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:26.680
Zoro. Why don't you relax?

19
00:02:26.710 --> 00:02:28.740
You're just wasting your energy doing that.

20
00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:29.940
Who asked you?

21
00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:32.720
Excuse him, Nami. He's hopeless.

22
00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:34.620
Guys like Zoro...
they gotta keep moving

23
00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:36.680
or they won't stay focused.

24
00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:39.050
They have one-track minds,
'specially...

25
00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:43.950
...our own resident
muscle-freak, here,

26
00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:46.620
now that he's had a taste of the Seven Warlords.

27
00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:48.380
Stop whining.

28
00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:51.610
Just say what's on
your mind, or shut up!

29
00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:53.980
Ah, you need me to spell it out?

30
00:02:54.010 --> 00:02:56.620
All this tough-guy bluster
is just a sad attempt

31
00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:59.320
to mask your fear that
Luffy might lose this one.

32
00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:00.350
Who, me?

33
00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:02.320
You sayin' I'm scared? Huh?

34
00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:04.360
Is that what you're sayin'?
Look at me!

35
00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:05.290
Fancy eyebrows!

36
00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:08.390
That's it!
I've had enough of you!

37
00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:09.800
Ya damn moss-head!

38
00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:11.500
What'd you call me?!

39
00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:13.130
You wanna go at it?

40
00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:15.990
Cut it out! This is pointless!

41
00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:17.330
She's strong!

42
00:03:19.030 --> 00:03:20.130
Look at 'em.

43
00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:22.400
They're at each other's throats.
Everyone's worked up.

44
00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:25.370
It's up to me, as vice-captain,
to take charge.

45
00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.500
Calm down! All of you!

46
00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:29.090
Everyone's frightened, yes,

47
00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:31.100
but we mustn't turn on each other!

48
00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:33.500
Luffy's counting on us to meet him in Alubarna!

49
00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:36.240
Yeah, well, you seem more
on-edge than any of us!

50
00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:42.110
Keep your mind on the rebellion
and leave the rest to us.

51
00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:44.010
Sorry about that, Vivi.

52
00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:47.810
If we tear each other apart, we've already lost.

53
00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:49.280
All right, that's settled.

54
00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:51.920
Now, let's devote our
attention to Alubarna!

55
00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:53.780
Full speed, Scissors!

56
00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:54.830
Huh?

57
00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:57.300
"Scissors"?

58
00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:58.500
Name for the crab.

59
00:03:58.540 --> 00:03:59.470
Oh!

60
00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:00.910
You just make that up?

61
00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:01.980
Got something better?

62
00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:02.940
No, not really.

63
00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:10.270
<b>Yuba
Former Rebel Base Camp</b>

64
00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:15.910
Water!
I can hardly believe my eyes.

65
00:04:17.410 --> 00:04:19.010
Precious water.

66
00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:22.410
The water is coming forth!

67
00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:26.650
Didn't I tell you, Luffy?

68
00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:30.520
This land is strong.

69
00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:36.530
Through it all, Yuba lives on.

70
00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:43.580
This sand storm
will deal Yuba a final,

71
00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:44.920
destructive blow.

72
00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:48.890
Fanning the flames of anger
within the rebel army

73
00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:51.110
until an inferno ignites.

74
00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:56.330
But in the end,
the bleeding hearts

75
00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:58.800
which infest this land
are what's killing it.

76
00:04:59.930 --> 00:05:04.330
And you, Straw Hat Luffy, are the worst of them all.

77
00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:07.270
If only you had purged yourself of such weakness,

78
00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:09.300
you may have lived a little longer.

79
00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:12.440
Water.

80
00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:17.550
I assume you don't feel so indebted to this water now.

81
00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:33.800
What's this? You're still alive?

82
00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:54.810
That looks like it hurts.

83
00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:57.440
But you'll be out of
your misery soon enough.

84
00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:07.500
Goodbye.

85
00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:15.780
That was a complete
waste of my time.

86
00:06:28.290 --> 00:06:29.530
Not so bad.

87
00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:31.360
Once we've weathered this storm,

88
00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:34.160
the rain will bless
us with sweet relief.

89
00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:35.570
Just like always.

90
00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:42.910
Your winds will never
vanquish us, you cowardly storm!

91
00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:45.540
Yuba will never give in to the sand!

92
00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:57.980
Me, go to Alubarna?

93
00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:01.420
Are we chasing after
the Straw Hat pirates?

94
00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:04.360
Or, uh, reinforcing
the royal army?

95
00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:05.490
That's up to you.

96
00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:09.460
You'll have to decide
which is more important

97
00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:10.760
when you get there.

98
00:07:10.790 --> 00:07:14.090
But Sir. I don't understand.
What's going on?

99
00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:16.060
Rely on your sense of justice.

100
00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:21.740
Whatever happens, I'll accept responsibility.

101
00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:24.640
Captain, where are you going?

102
00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:25.940
I have to head out to sea.

103
00:07:26.020 --> 00:07:27.960
Something unforeseen has come up.

104
00:07:27.990 --> 00:07:29.940
Be on alert to receive
communication from me

105
00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:31.080
at any time.

106
00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:32.850
Right!

107
00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:35.130
I need you to keep a
vigilant eye on this country

108
00:07:35.170 --> 00:07:36.640
and where it ends up.

109
00:07:39.590 --> 00:07:41.860
Whether it falls,
or whether it survives.

110
00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:44.060
The dawn of a brand
new and historic age

111
00:07:44.090 --> 00:07:45.560
is on the horizon.

112
00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:55.910
Sergeant Major. Sergeant Major!

113
00:07:55.970 --> 00:07:57.700
– Your orders?
– Yes.

114
00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:02.720
Whether it falls,
or whether it survives.

115
00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:04.960
The dawn of a brand
new and historic age

116
00:08:04.990 --> 00:08:06.430
is on the horizon.

117
00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:15.800
Our target is the
pirate Straw Hat Luffy,

118
00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:17.770
and everyone who
serves under him!

119
00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:21.910
All hands reinforce your gear!
Prepare to depart for Alubarna!

120
00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:22.940
– Right!
– Right!

121
00:08:24.580 --> 00:08:26.180
Straw Hat Luffy.

122
00:08:35.630 --> 00:08:36.660
Damn you, Cobra!

123
00:08:36.690 --> 00:08:39.160
My brethren and I are
willing to defend Alabasta

124
00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:41.630
with every last drop
of blood in our bodies.

125
00:08:41.670 --> 00:08:43.900
We will die before
turning it over to you!

126
00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:52.340
<b>Alubarna, the Capital</b>

127
00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:52.860
Hurry! Step lively!

128
00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:56.260
the southern gate!
Stop dawdling around and focus!

129
00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:58.230
We need more cannonballs over here!

130
00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:02.630
Chaka!

131
00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:07.270
The enemy's number is said
to be well over two million!

132
00:09:08.740 --> 00:09:10.880
Tell me, soldier, what do
you think of His Majesty's

133
00:09:10.910 --> 00:09:12.480
attack on Nanohana?

134
00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:14.740
I have served his Majesty
for over ten years

135
00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:16.570
and I was quite surprised.

136
00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:17.640
You're right.

137
00:09:17.670 --> 00:09:20.480
There's really no way anyone could rationalize it.

138
00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:23.500
Logic would suggest something
has happened to the king.

139
00:09:25.180 --> 00:09:26.080
If true...

140
00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:28.220
It is all the more reason
why we must not

141
00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:29.730
lose this fight.

142
00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:31.660
Bury your fear deep.

143
00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:33.580
For your King's sake.

144
00:09:33.610 --> 00:09:36.280
As well as that
of Princess Vivi!

145
00:09:36.310 --> 00:09:39.580
We will defend this
country at all cost!

146
00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:41.460
Everyone who is not prepared to fight

147
00:09:41.490 --> 00:09:43.290
take shelter outside the city!

148
00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:45.730
We cannot guarantee your
safety if you elect to stay!

149
00:09:45.760 --> 00:09:46.960
Run!

150
00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:49.900
If we don't get outta here,
we'll be in the line of fire!

151
00:09:51.010 --> 00:09:52.850
Things are getting
hectic down there,

152
00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:54.610
I see.

153
00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:57.440
But it's still moving too slow.
Hurry up and fight already!

154
00:09:57.480 --> 00:09:58.910
I can't stand waiting!

155
00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:06.490
I can't take this.
I really don't care if he is

156
00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:07.550
or isn't the king.

157
00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:09.400
I'm gonna go outta my mind
if I have to stand here

158
00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:10.830
guarding him any longer.

159
00:10:10.870 --> 00:10:13.700
Cant. Can't. Can't take this.

160
00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:15.650
Four!

161
00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:16.990
I mean, sure, slipping past

162
00:10:17.020 --> 00:10:18.790
the palace guards
and kidnapping this royal

163
00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:20.670
pain-in-the-rear is a
mission which only a team

164
00:10:20.670 --> 00:10:22.440
of our accomplished
skills could pull off.

165
00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:24.310
But, now that it's over,
this assignment has

166
00:10:24.340 --> 00:10:25.810
become a tedious bore!

167
00:10:25.840 --> 00:10:27.680
Right, Mr. 4?

168
00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:29.670
Did anything I said
manage to seep through

169
00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:32.220
that thick head of yours?
Slow, you're so slow.

170
00:10:33.550 --> 00:10:35.150
My back is killing me!

171
00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:37.330
Chaka. Koza.

172
00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:38.530
You mustn't fight.

173
00:10:38.550 --> 00:10:41.980
The two of you embody the spirit of this great country.

174
00:10:42.020 --> 00:10:44.520
Divided, you only weaken her resolve.

175
00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:49.490
There are those
who lament war...

176
00:10:55.010 --> 00:10:57.350
...and those
who race towards it.

177
00:11:04.740 --> 00:11:06.410
Just go ahead and run away.

178
00:11:06.440 --> 00:11:07.680
Four!

179
00:11:10.680 --> 00:11:13.880
Still, others incite war.

180
00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:16.350
But for the very few who know the truth,

181
00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:17.950
they strive to prevent it.

182
00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:22.380
These widely opposing viewpoints
all have one thing in common.

183
00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:22.410
<b>Alubarna</b>

184
00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:29.750
<b>Yuba</b>
<b>Erumalu</b>
<b>Katorea</b>
<b>Nanohana</b>

185
00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:22.700
<b>Rainbase</b>

186
00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:29.750
<b>Rainbase Alubarna</b>

187
00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:24.080
They are about to clash,

188
00:11:24.110 --> 00:11:26.680
here in the capital
city of Alubarna.

189
00:11:31.840 --> 00:11:32.780
What?!

190
00:11:32.810 --> 00:11:34.880
What do you mean we
can't cross this river?

191
00:11:34.910 --> 00:11:35.750
Think about it.

192
00:11:35.780 --> 00:11:37.650
Moving Crabs are
creatures of the desert.

193
00:11:37.680 --> 00:11:38.720
They don't take to water.

194
00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:40.470
Has everyone gone nuts?

195
00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:44.670
It's a crab! They can exist
on land and water!

196
00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:46.140
Guys, this is not good!

197
00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:48.000
This is a serious problem!
Look!

198
00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:49.830
If we just carelessly spend our energy

199
00:11:49.860 --> 00:11:52.540
swimming across the river,
we're not gonna make it in time!

200
00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:53.400
See here?

201
00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:55.000
After the river,
there's tons of desert

202
00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:56.070
to deal with!

203
00:11:56.100 --> 00:11:58.040
So, if this crab can't make it
to the other shore,

204
00:11:58.070 --> 00:12:00.670
are we supposed to run
the rest of the way on foot?

205
00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:01.820
We don't have a choice.

206
00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:03.760
We won't make it in time!

207
00:12:03.820 --> 00:12:05.990
It's absolutely impossible!

208
00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:15.430
Uh-oh. Hey, I can see it!

209
00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:17.070
Sandora River straight ahead!

210
00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:17.840
Oh, great.

211
00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:20.480
Help us, Scissors!
Pretty please!

212
00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:23.580
I know.
Scissors loves dancer girls.

213
00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:26.850
Will this do?

214
00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:27.520
Probably.

215
00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:29.360
Wow! I can't take it!

216
00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:33.460
He's looking this way!

217
00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:37.730
We're accelerating!

218
00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:39.770
Nami swan!

219
00:12:43.840 --> 00:12:45.870
Great! Now we've
got two animals in heat!

220
00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:47.840
All right! We're moving now!

221
00:12:49.510 --> 00:12:52.050
And what exactly
has this solved, Chopper?

222
00:12:52.210 --> 00:12:53.510
Nothing!

223
00:12:59.850 --> 00:13:01.020
Go faster!

224
00:13:04.590 --> 00:13:05.630
He did it!

225
00:13:06.430 --> 00:13:08.200
I'm seeing it,
but I don't believe it.

226
00:13:08.230 --> 00:13:09.900
This crab is incredible!

227
00:13:09.900 --> 00:13:11.870
Way to go!

228
00:13:11.900 --> 00:13:14.840
Now, don't you stop!
Just keep on going. Hurry!

229
00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:17.000
Run, run, run all the way!

230
00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:18.910
Go! Keep moving!

231
00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:21.540
Nothing can stop us now!
Oh! I love this crab!

232
00:13:21.580 --> 00:13:23.540
Hey, wait a minute!
What's going on?

233
00:13:23.580 --> 00:13:26.150
If I didn't know better,
I'd think we were sinking!

234
00:13:31.260 --> 00:13:33.000
You stupid crab!

235
00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:33.860
It's over.

236
00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:37.170
No use whining about it.
Keep moving.

237
00:13:37.220 --> 00:13:38.220
Hold on a second!

238
00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:40.220
Are you sure there aren't
any boats around here?

239
00:13:40.260 --> 00:13:42.100
How long will it take us to reach the shore?

240
00:13:42.100 --> 00:13:43.480
The rest of the night.

241
00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:44.780
That's insane!

242
00:13:46.820 --> 00:13:48.620
Thanks a lot!

243
00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:50.660
Thanks for the ride.
Bye, Scissors.

244
00:13:50.690 --> 00:13:53.490
Oh, shut up! He's the reason
we're in this mess!

245
00:13:56.560 --> 00:13:57.830
What the...?

246
00:14:00.450 --> 00:14:01.910
It's a Sandoran catfish!

247
00:14:01.950 --> 00:14:03.620
They're rarely seen by humans!

248
00:14:03.650 --> 00:14:05.620
Doesn't seem that rare to me!

249
00:14:06.750 --> 00:14:09.290
Did I mention they
love to eat human flesh?

250
00:14:09.320 --> 00:14:11.390
You could've
told us a bit sooner!

251
00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:22.670
Get off of me, dammit!
I can't see a thing

252
00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:26.180
with you hanging on
so tight! Chopper!

253
00:14:31.520 --> 00:14:33.560
Kung Fu Dugongs?

254
00:14:35.620 --> 00:14:36.950
They say they
were just looking out for

255
00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:38.390
their fellow pupils.

256
00:14:38.420 --> 00:14:39.360
Pupils?

257
00:14:39.390 --> 00:14:41.920
What, they think Luffy's
our master? Please.

258
00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:43.530
You really want
to argue with them?

259
00:14:43.560 --> 00:14:44.790
Hang in there, little guys!

260
00:14:44.830 --> 00:14:46.800
Just a little further!

261
00:14:46.840 --> 00:14:48.510
Thanks a lot!

262
00:14:48.530 --> 00:14:49.930
Bye-bye!

263
00:14:52.750 --> 00:14:54.020
Now that things are going smoothly,

264
00:14:54.050 --> 00:14:55.550
can we make it in time?

265
00:14:55.590 --> 00:14:56.450
I don't know.

266
00:14:56.490 --> 00:14:58.490
Even riding Eyelash,
I'm not sure when

267
00:14:58.560 --> 00:14:59.630
we would get there.

268
00:14:59.660 --> 00:15:01.700
Not to be pessimistic,
but Eyelash can only

269
00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:02.800
carry two of us.

270
00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:04.100
If Baroque Works
is going to attack us,

271
00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:06.700
it'll be from here on,
so we can't split up.

272
00:15:06.730 --> 00:15:09.140
Isn't there any way for us to stick together?

273
00:15:12.610 --> 00:15:14.210
Damn. This isn't good.

274
00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:19.020
Look! Over there!

275
00:15:19.050 --> 00:15:20.790
What is it now?
Is it the enemy?

276
00:15:20.820 --> 00:15:23.090
Don't tell me they're here to kill us already!

277
00:15:25.120 --> 00:15:27.090
No wait! That sound!

278
00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:28.640
Karoo!

279
00:15:28.640 --> 00:15:30.710
And the Supersonic
Duck Squadron!

280
00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:34.120
<b>Squadron Leader Karoo
Supersonic Duck Squad
(Swiftest Unit in Arabasta)</b>

281
00:15:35.770 --> 00:15:37.240
You've come to
help us, haven't you?

282
00:15:38.550 --> 00:15:39.580
Karoo!

283
00:16:01.820 --> 00:16:04.690
Meat!

284
00:16:12.230 --> 00:16:14.040
We may both be pirates.

285
00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:18.310
But you fall grossly
short on skill.

286
00:16:18.340 --> 00:16:20.910
This sand storm will
deal Yuba a final,

287
00:16:20.940 --> 00:16:22.780
destructive blow.

288
00:16:22.810 --> 00:16:25.310
Fanning the flames of anger
within the rebel army

289
00:16:25.350 --> 00:16:27.250
until an inferno ignites.

290
00:17:15.150 --> 00:17:16.820
Thank... Thank you.

291
00:17:22.420 --> 00:17:23.920
Why do you fight?

292
00:17:29.730 --> 00:17:31.700
Those of you with
the name of "D."

293
00:17:34.170 --> 00:17:35.240
"D"?

294
00:17:37.480 --> 00:17:38.940
Who are you people?

295
00:17:38.980 --> 00:17:40.410
What are your intentions?

296
00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:44.150
Apparently,
you don't have a clue

297
00:17:44.190 --> 00:17:45.750
what I'm talking about.

298
00:17:51.290 --> 00:17:52.430
I found you!

299
00:17:58.300 --> 00:18:00.260
Where is Vivi?

300
00:18:00.290 --> 00:18:01.290
My.

301
00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:04.950
Awake already?

302
00:18:04.990 --> 00:18:07.040
Now that I've
studied your ability,

303
00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:09.240
this won't turn out
like it did last time!

304
00:18:11.490 --> 00:18:12.960
Be careful, Pell.

305
00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:15.000
Don't wanna overexert yourself.

306
00:18:21.070 --> 00:18:22.400
Perfect timing.

307
00:18:22.440 --> 00:18:25.040
Why don't you save the boy before he dies?

308
00:18:27.860 --> 00:18:30.060
After all, if it weren't
for his courage

309
00:18:30.100 --> 00:18:33.160
and selflessness, who knows
if your precious princess

310
00:18:33.200 --> 00:18:35.230
would've made
it back alive at all.

311
00:18:35.270 --> 00:18:38.140
It must please you to know Vivi's safe.

312
00:18:38.100 --> 00:18:42.270
<b>Accelegator
The Second Fastest
Animal in Arabasta</b>

313
00:18:38.160 --> 00:18:41.100
That even as we speak, she's on her way to Alubarna.

314
00:18:41.130 --> 00:18:43.800
Though it's a long trip,
and anything could happen.

315
00:18:43.840 --> 00:18:46.040
Guess the situation is what it is.

316
00:19:00.150 --> 00:19:02.890
If I'm not able to
stop her, then who can?

317
00:19:02.920 --> 00:19:05.460
Vivi must be protected for everyone's sake!

318
00:19:11.230 --> 00:19:13.480
Meat!

319
00:19:12.710 --> 00:19:17.300
<b>Nanohana, a Port Town</b>

320
00:19:13.480 --> 00:19:16.490
So, the final revolt has begun.

321
00:19:16.520 --> 00:19:18.620
There was a lone ship.
Hopefully that means

322
00:19:18.660 --> 00:19:20.960
Princess Vivi and the others
were able to make it

323
00:19:20.990 --> 00:19:22.990
to Alabasta in one piece.

324
00:19:23.030 --> 00:19:26.060
I must hurry.
I pray there's still time.

325
00:19:28.110 --> 00:19:30.270
Hey, kid! Are you all right?

326
00:19:30.340 --> 00:19:31.610
Need meat!

327
00:19:34.440 --> 00:19:37.420
Meat.

328
00:19:37.450 --> 00:19:40.220
Meat? You don't need food now.

329
00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:42.190
That's the least of your worries.

330
00:19:42.220 --> 00:19:44.290
Hang on.
I'll get a doctor for you.

331
00:19:48.760 --> 00:19:52.630
I am going to make
sure Crocodile pays for this.

332
00:19:55.400 --> 00:19:58.100
He insulted Vivi,
and that old man

333
00:19:58.140 --> 00:20:01.210
with the shovel
who gave me water.

334
00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:03.460
He's definitely gonna pay!

335
00:20:06.210 --> 00:20:07.580
Who is this person?

336
00:20:09.920 --> 00:20:11.180
Meat.

337
00:20:32.970 --> 00:20:33.970
There it is!

338
00:20:33.970 --> 00:20:36.470
It's still in the distance, but it's Alubarna!

339
00:20:37.370 --> 00:20:39.970
Koza! We're less than
thirty minutes away.

340
00:20:39.970 --> 00:20:41.620
Yeah.

341
00:20:41.620 --> 00:20:44.340
We're nearing Alubarna now!

342
00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:46.410
The time has come, men!

343
00:20:51.640 --> 00:20:53.470
Chaka, we've sighted
the rebel army.

344
00:20:53.510 --> 00:20:55.410
They're about ten
miles to the south!

345
00:20:55.470 --> 00:20:57.410
Their forces are bearing
down on the southern gate

346
00:20:57.480 --> 00:20:58.840
as we speak!

347
00:20:58.880 --> 00:21:02.820
East. West. South.
Southeast. Southwest!

348
00:21:02.850 --> 00:21:05.200
Guard each gate with your life!

349
00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:08.530
Do not let even one of them set foot within our walls!

350
00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:09.540
– Right!
– Right!

351
00:21:20.510 --> 00:21:26.520
<b>West Gate, Alubarna</b>

352
00:21:25.350 --> 00:21:27.290
Hey, take a look over there!

353
00:21:27.320 --> 00:21:29.360
The rebel army is approaching!

354
00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:31.290
And there are so many of them!

355
00:21:31.320 --> 00:21:33.190
The princess is
such a little idiot

356
00:21:33.230 --> 00:21:34.560
to think she can stop them!

357
00:21:34.630 --> 00:21:37.330
But then, is the little idiot even coming?

358
00:21:37.380 --> 00:21:39.400
Really, now will she show up?

359
00:21:39.400 --> 00:21:43.330
Or will she not? Or will she?
Or will she not?

360
00:21:43.420 --> 00:21:44.560
The outcome is vague!

361
00:21:44.590 --> 00:21:46.260
What, what, what, what, what?

362
00:21:46.320 --> 00:21:48.390
Are we sure about this?
Shouldn't we be sure?

363
00:21:48.440 --> 00:21:50.240
The princess and the pirates
are really coming, right?

364
00:21:50.300 --> 00:21:52.330
At this rate, the rebel army
is going to beat them here!

365
00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:54.500
I thought those idiots wanted to stop the fighting!

366
00:21:54.540 --> 00:21:56.350
Shouldn't they at least try to be on time?

367
00:21:56.350 --> 00:21:57.650
I think it's entirely possible

368
00:21:57.680 --> 00:21:59.680
that they won't
make it soon enough.

369
00:21:59.680 --> 00:22:01.420
It might even be likely, really.

370
00:22:01.440 --> 00:22:02.880
After all, they did
lose precious time

371
00:22:02.880 --> 00:22:04.220
when they were in Rainbase.

372
00:22:04.240 --> 00:22:06.180
What? They did?

373
00:22:06.210 --> 00:22:08.180
All right, then.
Let's suppose the rebellion

374
00:22:08.220 --> 00:22:09.400
does get started first.

375
00:22:09.400 --> 00:22:12.470
What are we supposed to
deux if that does happen?

376
00:22:12.510 --> 00:22:15.080
We wouldn't have to "deux"
anything, would we?

377
00:22:15.110 --> 00:22:17.080
Think about it. Once the
rebellion gets under way,

378
00:22:17.120 --> 00:22:18.650
there's nothing even
the princess will be able

379
00:22:18.680 --> 00:22:20.150
to do to stop it.

380
00:22:20.190 --> 00:22:21.690
All we need to do is eliminate

381
00:22:21.760 --> 00:22:23.520
whoever we're told to.

382
00:22:23.590 --> 00:22:25.760
Can't you even manage
to figure that much out

383
00:22:25.790 --> 00:22:26.760
on your own?

384
00:22:26.790 --> 00:22:28.460
It sounds like
you're just dying to see

385
00:22:28.490 --> 00:22:29.690
some of my dance moves.

386
00:22:29.700 --> 00:22:32.100
Just calm down
and let it go, you two.

387
00:22:32.190 --> 00:22:33.490
My back. It hurts!

388
00:22:33.530 --> 00:22:35.430
Get over here and
massage it, Mr. 4!

389
00:22:35.450 --> 00:22:40.190
They're... com... ing... now.

390
00:22:40.220 --> 00:22:41.460
Really?!

391
00:22:41.500 --> 00:22:44.340
Why didn't you tell us
that earlier, you idiot?

392
00:22:47.900 --> 00:22:50.640
Ducks! They're on ducks?!

393
00:22:50.720 --> 00:22:52.320
They're on ducks?

394
00:22:52.350 --> 00:22:54.890
Are you sure?
Do you see anything else?

395
00:22:54.940 --> 00:22:56.780
Seems like their
number's gone up, too.

396
00:22:56.780 --> 00:22:58.110
There are six of 'em.

397
00:22:58.110 --> 00:22:59.210
With Straw Hat out of the way,

398
00:22:59.240 --> 00:23:02.610
I thought there was only
supposed to be four left.

399
00:23:02.610 --> 00:23:04.680
Not quite, Miss Merry Christmas.

400
00:23:04.740 --> 00:23:06.510
Don't you remember what the boss said?

401
00:23:06.540 --> 00:23:09.210
He told us there's that Mr. Prince guy, too.

402
00:23:09.240 --> 00:23:10.640
And apparently there's
more than one of him,

403
00:23:10.750 --> 00:23:12.580
so the numbers do add up.

404
00:23:12.620 --> 00:23:14.320
Just do the math.

405
00:23:14.320 --> 00:23:15.650
It doesn't matter.

406
00:23:15.650 --> 00:23:18.450
Vivi is our only target.

407
00:23:18.520 --> 00:23:21.320
What are you so worried about?

408
00:23:21.320 --> 00:23:23.590
Well, Mr. 1.

409
00:23:23.660 --> 00:23:27.660
You say Princess Vivi is the
only one we need to eliminate?

410
00:23:27.660 --> 00:23:28.660
Okay.

411
00:23:30.560 --> 00:23:32.230
Then how 'bout you
take a stab at guessing

412
00:23:32.260 --> 00:23:33.330
which one she is!

413
00:23:33.400 --> 00:23:36.740
They're all wearing
identical outfits!

414
00:23:38.770 --> 00:23:40.470
Even worse, those birds
are the quickest

415
00:23:40.560 --> 00:23:41.670
in the whole kingdom.

416
00:23:41.670 --> 00:23:43.410
Supersonic ducks!

417
00:23:48.450 --> 00:23:49.850
Those sneaky rats!

418
00:23:49.850 --> 00:23:51.880
How're we supposed
to tell which one is Vivi

419
00:23:51.880 --> 00:23:53.420
like this?

420
00:23:53.450 --> 00:23:56.220
It's just not a fair thing to do, you know?!

421
00:24:06.230 --> 00:24:08.300
Let them have it now, MR. 4!

422
00:24:12.270 --> 00:24:13.270
Dodge it!

423
00:24:16.390 --> 00:24:17.230
Missed them!

424
00:24:17.260 --> 00:24:19.260
Those damn birds!
They're too fast!

425
00:24:20.900 --> 00:24:22.660
Two just broke off from the rest!

426
00:24:22.660 --> 00:24:24.270
They're splitting up!

427
00:24:24.430 --> 00:24:26.800
Looks like they're planning
to go for the south gate.

428
00:24:26.800 --> 00:24:29.480
Those two are heading straight
toward the rebel army.

429
00:24:29.480 --> 00:24:31.920
Which means one
of them must be Vivi.

430
00:24:31.950 --> 00:24:34.460
We'll go ahead and
take care of those two.

431
00:24:34.490 --> 00:24:35.760
Move it, Mr. 4!

432
00:24:39.610 --> 00:24:41.780
Special attack! Fire star!

433
00:24:45.370 --> 00:24:47.300
Two more of them
are breaking off that way,

434
00:24:47.340 --> 00:24:49.670
Mr. 1. That could be Vivi.

435
00:24:49.700 --> 00:24:52.440
Seems they're planning to go in through the west gate.

436
00:24:52.480 --> 00:24:55.380
Damn brats. Let's go!

437
00:24:57.690 --> 00:24:59.520
Un... Deux!

438
00:24:59.560 --> 00:25:02.500
Okay! Let's head
for the southwest gate now!

439
00:25:05.320 --> 00:25:10.030
<b>West East</b>
<b>Southwest Southeast</b>
<b>South</b>

440
00:25:05.740 --> 00:25:06.970
So they're going to approach three

441
00:25:07.030 --> 00:25:10.400
of Alubarna's five
gates from the west?

442
00:25:10.030 --> 00:25:10.900
<b>West East</b>
<b>Southwest Southeast</b>
<b>South</b>

443
00:25:10.430 --> 00:25:11.900
If they're gonna split up and enter that way,

444
00:25:11.940 --> 00:25:13.040
then we'll do the same thing.

445
00:25:13.120 --> 00:25:14.820
We can wipe them
out inside the city!

446
00:25:16.440 --> 00:25:18.280
You're not getting away from me!

447
00:25:23.490 --> 00:25:24.920
Hey! Someone's coming!

448
00:25:24.960 --> 00:25:26.380
Is it the rebels?

449
00:25:26.380 --> 00:25:27.770
No, wait!

450
00:25:27.770 --> 00:25:29.770
It's the Supersonic
Duck Squadron!

451
00:25:29.770 --> 00:25:30.840
Let them in!

452
00:25:45.590 --> 00:25:46.860
I'm not kidding here!

453
00:25:46.890 --> 00:25:49.730
There's no way you're getting away with this!

454
00:25:49.760 --> 00:25:53.760
Four. Four. Four. Four.

455
00:26:02.640 --> 00:26:05.110
Tee hee hee! Thank you
so much for following us

456
00:26:05.180 --> 00:26:06.950
all the way here.

457
00:26:06.980 --> 00:26:08.010
Say what?

458
00:26:11.990 --> 00:26:13.220
Now! Stop!

459
00:26:14.220 --> 00:26:16.560
Wow, you guys
are very good, you know?

460
00:26:16.560 --> 00:26:18.730
That's right.
I'm the real Princess Vivi.

461
00:26:18.750 --> 00:26:21.260
What are you...I mean,
what are you talking about?

462
00:26:21.260 --> 00:26:23.730
I am the real Princess Vivi!

463
00:26:26.600 --> 00:26:28.860
I wonder if this
is far enough now.

464
00:26:33.240 --> 00:26:35.850
I have to say, it's
really entertaining how easily

465
00:26:35.880 --> 00:26:37.700
you all fell for this.

466
00:26:37.700 --> 00:26:41.070
Now. We can go ahead and
take these silly cloaks off.

467
00:26:42.970 --> 00:26:45.470
– Too bad! It looks like your guess was wrong!
– Too bad! It looks like your guess was wrong!

468
00:26:49.910 --> 00:26:51.550
– What?!
– What?!

469
00:26:58.150 --> 00:27:00.080
Thank you so much, everyone.

470
00:27:02.250 --> 00:27:03.760
I have to hurry now.

471
00:27:03.760 --> 00:27:05.720
The rebel army
is almost to the city!

472
00:27:07.590 --> 00:27:08.890
Let's go, Karoo!

473
00:27:10.650 --> 00:27:12.620
Camel?!

474
00:27:12.620 --> 00:27:15.620
And I recognize you from the ship, too, don't I?

475
00:27:15.620 --> 00:27:17.590
Sorry!

476
00:27:17.620 --> 00:27:19.130
Yeah, come on, Zoro,
let 'em have it!

477
00:27:19.160 --> 00:27:21.230
Would you keep quiet over there?

478
00:27:21.250 --> 00:27:23.150
They fooled us.

479
00:27:23.220 --> 00:27:24.150
Quite a farce.

480
00:27:24.220 --> 00:27:26.620
I don't owe that
anymore! You cleared me!

481
00:27:26.660 --> 00:27:29.730
It looks like there
won't be any rebellion now.

482
00:27:29.760 --> 00:27:31.460
What did you say?

483
00:27:34.130 --> 00:27:36.230
I have to stop them at any cost.

484
00:27:36.270 --> 00:27:39.770
If I don't, then all of this
struggling has been for nothing!

485
00:27:41.030 --> 00:27:43.070
Whatever the cost,
Vivi and her friends

486
00:27:43.130 --> 00:27:45.030
must be prevented
from making contact

487
00:27:45.070 --> 00:27:46.500
with the rebel army.

488
00:27:53.830 --> 00:27:55.500
Secure the cannonballs!

489
00:27:55.530 --> 00:27:57.370
I don't want them rolling away!

490
00:27:57.440 --> 00:27:58.700
You heard him, men!

491
00:27:58.770 --> 00:28:01.710
Man your posts! Keep the
artillery under control!

492
00:28:02.840 --> 00:28:04.680
The ground is really moving, huh?

493
00:28:04.710 --> 00:28:07.680
The enemy army is made up of two million angry men.

494
00:28:07.680 --> 00:28:10.050
Even the ground shakes a little before them.

495
00:28:10.110 --> 00:28:11.450
Stay strong!

496
00:28:22.670 --> 00:28:24.840
It's okay, Karoo,
you don't have to be here.

497
00:28:28.610 --> 00:28:31.510
You could get trampled, so just be careful.

498
00:28:42.790 --> 00:28:43.960
Please, Leader.

499
00:28:43.990 --> 00:28:45.820
Please listen to what I have to say.

500
00:28:45.860 --> 00:28:47.460
You must hear it.

501
00:28:52.800 --> 00:28:54.200
Everyone listen!

502
00:28:54.240 --> 00:28:56.210
Close your ranks and stay together!

503
00:28:56.240 --> 00:28:58.940
We'll knock through the guards at the southern gate!

504
00:28:58.940 --> 00:29:01.210
The rest will fall from there!

505
00:29:01.240 --> 00:29:03.280
Do not lose heart!

506
00:29:11.560 --> 00:29:13.960
Rebel army, you must stop!

507
00:29:13.990 --> 00:29:16.830
This fight is pointless!
It's all a set-up!

508
00:29:19.960 --> 00:29:22.800
Please slow down!
You have got to listen to me!

509
00:29:34.640 --> 00:29:36.970
Hey! Did you see a person
standing in front of us

510
00:29:37.000 --> 00:29:37.870
just now?

511
00:29:37.870 --> 00:29:38.570
Person?

512
00:29:38.570 --> 00:29:40.210
That isn't important right now!

513
00:29:40.240 --> 00:29:42.510
The enemy is already shooting at us!

514
00:29:47.080 --> 00:29:48.220
Why did they do that?

515
00:29:48.370 --> 00:29:50.340
Neither side can see anything now!

516
00:29:53.070 --> 00:29:54.970
What is the royal army thinking?

517
00:29:56.870 --> 00:29:57.770
What the hell?!

518
00:29:57.810 --> 00:30:00.610
I haven't given anyone the order to open fire!

519
00:30:00.610 --> 00:30:02.240
Do not act without my say-so!

520
00:30:02.280 --> 00:30:05.050
Uh, sir!
I'm terribly sorry about that!

521
00:30:05.110 --> 00:30:07.620
I guess my hand just slipped!
Sorry!

522
00:30:28.100 --> 00:30:29.170
Don't back down!

523
00:30:29.170 --> 00:30:30.200
Charge through!

524
00:30:30.270 --> 00:30:32.310
It's just a cloud of sand.

525
00:30:32.340 --> 00:30:35.850
No, everyone!
You have to stop now!

526
00:30:37.140 --> 00:30:39.850
We'll make the king pay!

527
00:30:39.850 --> 00:30:40.880
Leader!

528
00:30:50.690 --> 00:30:52.790
Leader!

529
00:31:00.680 --> 00:31:02.180
Koza. What is it?

530
00:31:02.180 --> 00:31:04.020
Nothing. It's nothing.

531
00:31:06.320 --> 00:31:07.690
Was I imagining it?

532
00:31:21.870 --> 00:31:22.870
Leader.

533
00:31:24.930 --> 00:31:25.900
Remember, men!

534
00:31:25.930 --> 00:31:27.790
Today will be our final battle!

535
00:31:30.420 --> 00:31:31.790
Wait! Listen to me!

536
00:31:34.760 --> 00:31:36.730
Leader!

537
00:31:53.350 --> 00:31:54.480
They're here!

538
00:31:55.650 --> 00:31:57.420
Cannons ready!

539
00:32:02.990 --> 00:32:05.830
Fire!

540
00:32:23.000 --> 00:32:24.270
Save the country!

541
00:32:25.810 --> 00:32:27.950
Tear down Alubarna!

542
00:32:56.430 --> 00:32:58.400
No, Karoo!

543
00:33:01.400 --> 00:33:02.470
Karoo!

544
00:33:06.660 --> 00:33:08.560
You shielded me from them.

545
00:33:11.770 --> 00:33:13.400
I'm sorry.

546
00:33:13.440 --> 00:33:15.140
We've come so far.

547
00:33:15.170 --> 00:33:19.780
We've done so much,
but the rebellion has started.

548
00:33:19.860 --> 00:33:21.400
I'm so sorry.

549
00:33:21.460 --> 00:33:23.060
But I will still stop it.

550
00:33:23.170 --> 00:33:25.840
No matter how many times they refuse to listen.

551
00:33:26.030 --> 00:33:28.180
No matter how loudly I have to yell.

552
00:33:28.180 --> 00:33:30.220
I will not let mindless
fighting destroy

553
00:33:30.300 --> 00:33:32.100
what we've worked so hard for.

554
00:33:32.140 --> 00:33:36.190
That's something I learned
while I was onboard the ship.

555
00:33:36.190 --> 00:33:37.760
Do not ever give up.

556
00:33:40.810 --> 00:33:42.140
Vivi!

557
00:33:43.780 --> 00:33:45.480
At last! I found you!

558
00:33:45.550 --> 00:33:46.950
Usopp!

559
00:33:46.980 --> 00:33:48.720
We can still make it in time!

560
00:33:48.750 --> 00:33:49.990
Hurry and hop on!

561
00:33:50.040 --> 00:33:50.980
Right!

562
00:33:51.020 --> 00:33:52.560
Hang in there, Karoo!

563
00:33:52.620 --> 00:33:54.120
Oh, forget about that bird.

564
00:33:56.160 --> 00:33:59.060
What's the matter, Vivi? Come
on. We need to get going now!

565
00:33:59.060 --> 00:34:00.230
Hurry it up!

566
00:34:03.830 --> 00:34:06.870
That... bird?

567
00:34:10.140 --> 00:34:11.740
Let's go, Karoo!

568
00:34:16.360 --> 00:34:17.100
Come on!

569
00:34:17.170 --> 00:34:19.380
The rebellion will
only get worse.

570
00:34:22.110 --> 00:34:24.280
Usopp...

571
00:34:24.350 --> 00:34:26.250
Prove yourself.

572
00:34:26.270 --> 00:34:27.930
Hm? Really?

573
00:34:27.930 --> 00:34:29.700
You don't believe that it's me?

574
00:34:31.720 --> 00:34:32.820
See?

575
00:34:32.850 --> 00:34:33.890
No!

576
00:34:35.820 --> 00:34:37.720
Usopp! Hey, Usopp!

577
00:34:37.790 --> 00:34:39.690
Eyelash! Wake up!

578
00:34:39.720 --> 00:34:41.660
Oh, it's you, Sanji!

579
00:34:41.700 --> 00:34:43.000
Is it morning already?

580
00:34:43.040 --> 00:34:44.300
Uh, sure.

581
00:34:44.340 --> 00:34:46.710
So, this is how
our fight turned out.

582
00:34:46.740 --> 00:34:48.640
The part of the mission
where we lured them away

583
00:34:48.680 --> 00:34:50.840
went really well,
but then...

584
00:34:50.880 --> 00:34:52.810
Well, you see...

585
00:34:52.850 --> 00:34:54.680
Then it was over in two seconds.

586
00:34:54.720 --> 00:34:56.680
One second each.

587
00:34:56.820 --> 00:34:58.320
You couldn't have held out longer?

588
00:35:00.150 --> 00:35:02.190
What are you doing here anyway?

589
00:35:02.250 --> 00:35:03.090
Your ducks got me.

590
00:35:03.120 --> 00:35:05.160
They came to get some help for you two.

591
00:35:05.190 --> 00:35:06.360
But that aside...

592
00:35:06.360 --> 00:35:08.920
You let Mr. 2 get
away, didn't you?

593
00:35:08.920 --> 00:35:09.920
Yeah.

594
00:35:15.030 --> 00:35:16.100
Listen up.

595
00:35:16.100 --> 00:35:18.670
That creepy ballerina's transformations are perfect.

596
00:35:18.700 --> 00:35:19.940
There's no telling
when he might pose

597
00:35:20.000 --> 00:35:22.240
as one of us and make
an attempt on Vivi's life.

598
00:35:22.270 --> 00:35:24.370
Does everyone understand?

599
00:35:24.430 --> 00:35:27.200
If you ever feel like one of us is acting suspicious...

600
00:35:29.800 --> 00:35:31.270
...ask them to take
off this wrapping,

601
00:35:31.300 --> 00:35:32.700
reveal their mark.

602
00:35:32.740 --> 00:35:34.890
If they can't do that,
they're an imposter.

603
00:35:34.890 --> 00:35:35.890
Whoa.

604
00:35:35.890 --> 00:35:37.790
Having such a well
thought out plan like this

605
00:35:37.820 --> 00:35:40.630
seems uncharacteristically
smart for you.

606
00:35:40.640 --> 00:35:43.640
So how can we be sure you aren't already an imposter?

607
00:35:43.700 --> 00:35:44.730
I'll stab you!

608
00:35:44.800 --> 00:35:46.170
Yeah, that's him.

609
00:35:46.180 --> 00:35:48.180
Whew! Definitely Zoro.

610
00:35:54.910 --> 00:35:56.340
You're lying.

611
00:35:56.380 --> 00:35:58.140
You're not really Usopp.

612
00:35:59.830 --> 00:36:01.830
Well, that's too bad.

613
00:36:03.260 --> 00:36:06.830
Now, really! You knew? How?

614
00:36:06.900 --> 00:36:10.400
I thought my imitation was perfect.

615
00:36:10.440 --> 00:36:12.340
We even had a helpful report from the boss

616
00:36:12.340 --> 00:36:14.170
that you all had the same
bandages wrapped up

617
00:36:14.170 --> 00:36:15.810
on your arm like this.

618
00:36:15.840 --> 00:36:17.080
So smart of you.

619
00:36:18.980 --> 00:36:20.180
This isn't good.

620
00:36:21.920 --> 00:36:23.350
Vivi's in danger!
